course: dictionary
lesson: 1397
title: One word, many meanings: caravan
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The words around a word are its context, and they show you which meaning the writer wants. «Traders travelled in caravans of camels» tells you a caravan is a group of travellers moving together, because travellers and camels are the clues.
explain: Now read «Before the car, Toad tries a horse-drawn caravan holiday.» Here a caravan is a vehicle with beds and a kitchen, pulled along for a holiday. The word holiday is the clue. Ask yourself which meaning fits, then swap it into the sentence to check.
explain: Caravan can also be a verb in the UK. Caravanning means going on a holiday in a caravan. The -ing ending is a clue that someone is doing it. When you meet a word with more than one meaning, a dictionary tells you all of them.
fact: A caravan is a vehicle with beds and a kitchen, pulled by a car for holidays (UK, Australia, New Zealand). In the US it is called a trailer or RV.
fact: A caravan can also be a group of people travelling together, often with animals or vehicles, especially across a desert.
fact: «Caravans of two-humped Bactrian camels crossed cold deserts» means groups of camels with travellers, moving from one oasis to the next.
fact: Caravanning (UK) means going on a caravan holiday.
fact: Old caravans were covered wagons that people lived in, like a Romany caravan.
exercise: «Traders travelled in caravans of camels across the desert.» What is a caravan here? | A covered wagon that people lived in | A vehicle with beds and a kitchen, for holidays | A shop in a market | *A group of travellers and animals moving together
exercise: «Before the car, Toad tries a horse-drawn caravan holiday.» Which meaning fits this sentence? | A group of camels crossing a desert | A wagon with a painted roof, where a family lives | *A vehicle with beds and a kitchen, used for a holiday | A set of traders selling salt
exercise: In the UK, what does caravanning mean? | *Going on a holiday in a caravan | Selling vehicles at a market | Painting a covered wagon | Crossing a desert with camels
test: «Caravans of two-humped Bactrian camels crossed cold deserts from one oasis to the next.» In this sentence, what is a caravan? | A vehicle with beds for a holiday | A house with wheels for one family | *A group of travellers with animals, moving together | A camel with two humps
test: Grandad says he is caravanning in Cornwall this summer. What is he going to do? | Go to the desert on a camel | *Go on a holiday in a caravan | Live in a covered wagon for ever | Sell his car
exam: In the US, what would people call a caravan used for holidays? | A desert trader | A camel | *A trailer or RV | A covered wagon
